  <static seed="2128" source="Contrib/PCC/BasicAlgebra/NumberBasics/TypesOfNumbers50.pg">
    <statement><p>Which of the following are real numbers?  There may be more than
one correct answer.</p>
<p><var form="checkboxes">
<li>
<p><m>-7.7\overline{81}</m></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>92195</m></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>-{\frac{7}{34}}</m></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>-36687</m></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>-2</m></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>\pi</m></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>3.101001000100001\ldots</m></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>0</m></p>
</li>
</var></p>
</statement>
    <solution><p>All of these numbers are real numbers, since they can all be located on a number line.</p>
</solution>
